    "findings": [],
    "checks": [
      "ASCII start/continuation rules are identical across editions and checked before table lookup. NameStart accepts colon/underscore/letters; NameChar also accepts digits/hyphen/period. Empty names and multiple namespace separators remain rejected by the existing name/qname structure.",
      "partition_point searches the first range whose end is not smaller than the scalar; the subsequent start comparison rejects gaps. Verified ascending, disjoint ranges make this lookup correct. Scalars above u16 are rejected for Fourth Edition and continue through the existing Fifth Edition production for that mode.",
      "representative deliberately selects its class only after checking scalar.is_ascii(). Both editions have identical ASCII classes, while U+00C0 and U+00B7 representatives belong to the corresponding classes in both editions. Non-ASCII converted characters retain their actual scalar and therefore receive the selected edition classification at the consuming scanner.",
      "custom_public_byte now applies the selected NameRules to the custom map target only in the raw-ASCII remapping case, matching the earlier provenance byte-type model. Literal permitted public-ID bytes retain the unchanged fast path.",
      "This review excludes broad child/scanner policy propagation, which the API owner is auditing separately."
    ],
    "verdict": "No blocker found in the reviewed table and raw/decoded boundary logic.",
